---
const friction = [
  ['01', 'A decision takes five meetings because no one owns the trade-off.'],
  ['02', 'Roadmap changes feel like execution failure when the constraint is upstream.'],
  ['03', 'Product, revenue and delivery are all moving—just not in the same direction.'],
];
const stages = [
  ['TRACE', 'Map where a decision loses its owner, its evidence, or its consequence.'],
  ['LOCATE', 'Separate the visible delivery symptom from the operating constraint that produces it.'],
  ['TEST', 'Run a narrow intervention against the constraint before recommending broad change.'],
  ['INSTALL', 'Give the team a decision practice that survives the next urgent quarter.'],
];
const offers = [
  ['01', 'DECISION-FLOW ASSESSMENT', 'A concentrated diagnostic for a specific product or operating bottleneck.'],
  ['02', 'CONSTRAINT SPRINT', 'A scoped engagement to test and remove the constraint the assessment identifies.'],
  ['03', 'OPERATING REVIEW', 'A leadership working session for teams deciding what must change next.'],
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Dr. Marcus Hill — Niche Specialist | AURA Concept</title>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="description" content="A concept-safe Niche Specialist diagnostic-assessment preview compiled by AURA." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,600;9..40,700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body class="niche-preview">
    <a class="ns-skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="ns-header">
      <a href="/archetypes/niche-specialist/" class="ns-wordmark">MARCUS HILL<span>DECISION-FLOW ADVISORY</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Preview navigation"><a href="#diagnostic">THE DIAGNOSTIC</a><a href="#method">METHOD</a><a href="#services">ENGAGEMENTS</a></nav>
      <a href="#assessment" class="ns-header-cta">START ASSESSMENT <b>→</b></a>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="ns-hero">
        <div class="ns-grid-overlay"></div>
        <img src="/images/niche-specialist-hero.webp" alt="Conceptual B2B operations adviser standing beside an abstract decision-flow map." width="1920" height="1080" />
        <div class="ns-hero-copy">
          <p class="ns-label"><i></i> NICHE SPECIALIST / CONCEPT PREVIEW</p>
          <h1>YOUR TEAM<br />IS NOT <span>SLOW.</span><br />YOUR DECISIONS<br />ARE <em>EXPENSIVE.</em></h1>
          <p class="ns-intro">A diagnostic for B2B software leaders who have product-market fit—and a delivery system that no longer moves at the speed of their decisions.</p>
          <div class="ns-hero-actions"><a class="ns-primary" href="#assessment">START A DECISION-FLOW ASSESSMENT <b>→</b></a><a class="ns-secondary" href="#method">SEE THE DIAGNOSTIC METHOD <b>↓</b></a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ns-coordinate">SYSTEM: DECISION-FLOW / VER: 01.0<br />CONSTRAINT-FIRST OPERATING REVIEW</div>
      </section>

      <section class="ns-concept"><span>CONCEPT-SAFE PREVIEW</span><p>Dr. Marcus Hill, the photography, the diagnostic method and all operating contexts are fictional AURA test material. This page demonstrates the compiled <strong>Niche Specialist</strong> motion—not live client proof, results, or endorsements.</p></section>

      <section class="ns-friction" id="diagnostic">
        <div class="ns-sidebar"><span>01</span><p>THE COST OF<br />UNCLEAR FLOW</p></div>
        <div class="ns-friction-main" data-reveal>
          <p class="ns-label">THE DIAGNOSTIC QUESTION</p>
          <h2>WHERE DOES A<br />GOOD DECISION<br /><em>GO TO DIE?</em></h2>
          <p class="ns-friction-lede">The first task is not to improve every meeting. It is to find the specific place where a decision loses clarity, ownership, or consequence.</p>
          <div class="ns-friction-list">{friction.map(([number, body]) => <article><span>{number}</span><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ns-method" id="method">
        <div class="ns-method-head"><div><p class="ns-label">THE DECISION-FLOW DIAGNOSTIC</p><h2>THE WORK IS<br />NOT TO <em>ADD</em><br />PROCESS.</h2></div><p>It is to make the existing system legible enough to see the constraint, test a move, and install a decision practice that remains useful once the consultant leaves.</p></div>
        <div class="ns-method-image"><img src="/images/niche-specialist-artifact.webp" alt="Conceptual operational adviser tracing a physical decision-flow map." width="1600" height="1067" /><div><span>ARTIFACT ROLE P09</span><p>A physical map replaces abstract opinions with an inspectable operating surface.</p></div></div>
        <div class="ns-stages">{stages.map(([title, body], index) => <article data-reveal><span>0{index + 1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div>
      </section>

      <section class="ns-proof">
        <div class="ns-proof-ink"><span>02</span><p>PROOF IS A<br />STANDARD,<br />NOT A DECORATION.</p></div>
        <div class="ns-proof-main" data-reveal><p class="ns-label">THE EVIDENCE POLICY</p><h2>NO CLAIM<br />WITHOUT A<br /><em>TRACE.</em></h2><p>For a real client site, the compiler requires a permissioned case anatomy: the starting constraint, operating context, intervention, observed outcome, and an approved right to publish it. Until then, the visual system carries the point of view—not invented receipts.</p><div class="ns-proof-checks"><span>✓ SPECIFIC DIAGNOSIS</span><span>✓ PERMISSIONED CONTEXT</span><span>✓ OBSERVABLE CHANGE</span><span>✓ APPROVED CLAIM ID</span></div></div>
      </section>

      <section class="ns-fieldwork"><img src="/images/niche-specialist-fieldwork.webp" alt="Conceptual adviser reviewing abstract operational flow marks on a glass board." width="1920" height="1080" /><div class="ns-fieldwork-copy"><span>ROLE P05 / OPERATIONAL FIELDWORK</span><h2>THE<br /><em>CONSTRAINT</em><br />IS ALWAYS<br />SOMEWHERE.</h2><p>Fieldwork is a role, not a stock-photo category. It visually proves the adviser’s relationship to the work without fabricating a client outcome.</p></div></section>

      <section class="ns-services" id="services">
        <div class="ns-services-top"><p class="ns-label">ENGAGEMENT PATHS</p><h2>START WHERE<br />THE <em>FLOW</em><br />BREAKS.</h2></div>
        <div class="ns-service-list">{offers.map(([number, title, body]) => <article><span>{number}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></div><a href="#assessment" aria-label={`Ask about ${title}`}>→</a></article>)}</div>
      </section>

      <section class="ns-assessment" id="assessment">
        <div class="ns-assessment-copy" data-reveal><p class="ns-label">START AN ASSESSMENT</p><h2>NAME THE<br /><em>CONSTRAINT.</em></h2><p>Share the operating context. The form is intentionally short, but it asks for the facts needed to decide whether a diagnostic is the right next step.</p><img src="/images/niche-specialist-conversation.webp" alt="Conceptual adviser in a private diagnostic conversation." width="1200" height="1500" /></div>
        <form action="#" method="post" class="ns-form" data-demo-form><p>Concept preview only. This form collects nothing; the field set comes directly from the compiled Niche Specialist assessment contract.</p><label>YOUR NAME<input name="name" placeholder="Name" /></label><label>WORK EMAIL<input name="email" type="email" placeholder="you@company.com" /></label><label>COMPANY<input name="company" placeholder="Company" /></label><div class="ns-form-pair"><label>BUSINESS TYPE<input name="business_type" placeholder="B2B software, platform…" /></label><label>SCALE<input name="scale" placeholder="Team / revenue band" /></label></div><div class="ns-form-pair"><label>TIMING<input name="timing" placeholder="When does this matter?" /></label><label>SERVICE NEED<input name="service_need" placeholder="Assessment / sprint / review" /></label></div><button type="submit">START A DECISION-FLOW ASSESSMENT <b>→</b></button></form>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="ns-footer"><span>MARCUS HILL / AURA NICHE SPECIALIST CONCEPT</span><span>COMPILED FROM A CONCEPT-SAFE CLIENT PACK</span></footer>
    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-demo-form]').forEach((form) => form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => { event.preventDefault(); alert('Concept preview only — no information is collected. A live client build connects this validated assessment field set to the approved contact backend.'); }));
      const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => entries.forEach((entry) => entry.isIntersecting && entry.target.setAttribute('data-visible', 'true')), { threshold: .1 });
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-reveal]').forEach((element) => observer.observe(element));
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

